IMPORT prelude

-- Immigration Act 1959 (Singapore) -- harbouring, employing and sheltering immigration offenders, worksite
-- occupiers, marriages of convenience, false information, and composition: ss 57 to 59.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Immigration Act 1959 -- offences`

§§ `57(1)(d), (7) to (7D) -- harbouring`

-- s 57(1)(d): harbouring a person "(i) whom the defendant KNOWS has acted in contravention ...; (ii) with RECKLESS
-- disregard ...; or (iii) NEGLIGENTLY failing to ascertain".
-- (1AA)(e): (i) and (ii) -- "a presumptive minimum term of not less than 6 months and not more than 2 years" and up to
-- $6,000. (f): (iii) -- $6,000 or 12 months or both.
-- (7): proof that the defendant "has given shelter to an immigration offender" raises a presumption of recklessness or
-- negligence. (7A): a pass is no defence unless the defendant proves due diligence that it was valid "at the material
-- time". (7C): due diligence means, for (ii), any TWO of the (7D) acts; for (iii), ALL THREE. (7D): (a) inspecting the
-- permit or pass; (b) checking that the passport particulars match it; (c) checking with the Controller (or the
-- Controller of Work Passes) that it was valid, or with the named employer.
-- (13): "immigration offender" means a person who contravened s 6(1), s 15 or s 36(1) or the regulations.
--
-- A landlord who lets a room to a foreign worker, inspects the pass and matches it to the passport, has done two of
-- three checks: enough to escape the recklessness charge, not enough to escape the negligence charge (s 7B lets the
-- prosecution fall back to it). Only the third check -- with the Controller or the employer -- completes the defence.
DECLARE Harbouring HAS
    `gave shelter to an immigration offender` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew the person was an offender` IS A BOOLEAN
    `inspected the permit or pass` IS A BOOLEAN
    `checked it against the passport` IS A BOOLEAN
    `checked validity with the Controller or the employer` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A Harbouring
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of due diligence checks done` MEANS
      (IF `the facts`'s `inspected the permit or pass` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF `the facts`'s `checked it against the passport` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF `the facts`'s `checked validity with the Controller or the employer` THEN 1 ELSE 0)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A Harbouring
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defendant is liable for knowing or reckless harbouring` IF
        `the facts`'s `gave shelter to an immigration offender`
    AND (    `the facts`'s `knew the person was an offender`
         OR  `the number of due diligence checks done` `the facts` LESS THAN 2)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A Harbouring
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defendant is liable for negligent harbouring` IF
        `the facts`'s `gave shelter to an immigration offender`
    AND `the number of due diligence checks done` `the facts` LESS THAN 3

-- In months.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A Harbouring
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the presumptive minimum imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `the defendant is liable for knowing or reckless harbouring` `the facts` THEN 6 ELSE 0

§§ `57(1)(e), (1A), (8) to (10) -- employing immigration offenders`

-- (1)(e): employing a person who contravened s 6(1), 15 or 36(1) -- presumptive minimum 6 months to 2 years, fine up
-- to $6,000. (1A): employing MORE THAN 5 at the same time -- caning in addition.
-- (8): "Where an immigration offender is found at any premises or place, other than premises used solely for
-- residential purposes, the occupier ... is PRESUMED ... to have employed him or her knowing that he or she is an
-- immigration offender."
-- (9), (10): a pass is no defence unless the employer inspected it, matched it to the passport, and -- for a visit pass
-- holder -- had reasonable grounds to believe a work pass was in force or the Controller had consented.
DECLARE Employment HAS
    `offenders employed at the same time` IS A NUMBER
    `inspected the pass` IS A BOOLEAN
    `matched it to the passport` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the worker held only a visit pass` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had reasonable grounds to believe a work pass or consent existed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the employment` IS AN Employment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer proved due diligence` IF
        `the employment`'s `inspected the pass`
    AND `the employment`'s `matched it to the passport`
    AND (    NOT `the employment`'s `the worker held only a visit pass`
         OR  `the employment`'s `had reasonable grounds to believe a work pass or consent existed`)

GIVEN `the employment` IS AN Employment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is liable` IF
        `the employment`'s `offenders employed at the same time` AT LEAST 1
    AND NOT `the employer proved due diligence` `the employment`

GIVEN `the employment` IS AN Employment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `caning is added` IF
        `the employer is liable` `the employment`
    AND `the employment`'s `offenders employed at the same time` GREATER THAN 5

GIVEN `found at premises used solely for residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupier is presumed to have employed the offender knowingly` IF
    NOT `found at premises used solely for residence`

§§ `57A -- construction sites`

-- s 57A(1): the occupier of a construction work place (the principal contractor) "must not permit any immigration
-- offender to enter or remain". (2): where one is found there, control, permission and KNOWLEDGE are all presumed.
-- (3), (4): rebutted only by proving all reasonable measures including those prescribed.
-- (6): a fine "of not less than $15,000 and not more than $30,000" or up to 12 months, or both, "FOR EACH immigration
-- offender found"; on a second conviction $30,000 to $60,000 or 2 years, for each.
GIVEN `offenders found` IS A NUMBER, `second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum fine if a fine is imposed` MEANS
    IF `second or subsequent conviction` THEN `offenders found` TIMES 30000 ELSE `offenders found` TIMES 15000

GIVEN `offenders found` IS A NUMBER, `second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `second or subsequent conviction` THEN `offenders found` TIMES 60000 ELSE `offenders found` TIMES 30000

§§ `57C -- marriages of convenience`

-- s 57C(1): a person who enters a marriage "(a) knowing or having reason to believe that the purpose of the marriage is
-- to assist one of the parties ... to obtain an immigration advantage; AND (b) where any GRATIFICATION ... is offered,
-- given or received as an inducement or reward" -- $10,000 or 10 YEARS. (2): a person who ARRANGES such a marriage
-- "with the intention of assisting" a party to obtain an immigration advantage -- the same, with NO gratification
-- requirement. (3): marriages inside or outside Singapore. (4): defence -- the defendant "believed on reasonable grounds
-- ... that the marriage would result in a genuine marital relationship".
--
-- The parties commit the offence only if gratification passed. The arranger commits it without any. So a broker who
-- introduces a couple for no fee, intending one to get a pass, is guilty where the couple, who exchanged nothing, are not.
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `a party to the marriage`
    `an arranger`

DECLARE MarriageFacts HAS
    `the role` IS A Role
    `knew or had reason to believe a purpose was an immigration advantage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gratification was offered, given or received for the marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `believed on reasonable grounds it would be a genuine marriage` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A MarriageFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the marriage of convenience offence` IF
        `the facts`'s `knew or had reason to believe a purpose was an immigration advantage`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `believed on reasonable grounds it would be a genuine marriage`
    AND CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the role`
        WHEN `a party to the marriage` THEN `the facts`'s `gratification was offered, given or received for the marriage`
        WHEN `an arranger` THEN TRUE

§§ `57(1)(k), (ka) -- false information`

-- (k): obtaining a permit or pass by information the person KNOWS is false or misleading -- $8,000 or 12 months.
-- (ka): the same by information that IS false or misleading -- "a strict liability offence" (1AAA) -- $4,000.
--
-- An applicant who honestly gets a date wrong on a form has committed the (ka) offence.
GIVEN `the information was false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person knew` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for the false information` MEANS
    IF NOT `the information was false or misleading in a material particular` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the person knew` THEN 8000 ELSE 4000

§§ `58, 59 -- general penalty and composition`

-- s 58: $2,000 or 6 months. s 59(1): a prescribed offence may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding $2,000".
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that can be collected on composition` MEANS 2000
